[3.021, "o", "8;2;153;153;153mSENSOR eslint: FAIL (2 findings)\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153msrc/domain/command.ts:38:7 ERROR @typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  Missing return type on function.\u001b[41G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  MISSING-RETURN-TYPE\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B  Write the type you intended, not the one the checker infers. Where the two differ, the difference is usually the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mbug.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  If the honest return type is a union of unrelated shapes, that is the real finding: Introduce Special Case, or \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153msplit into two functions with two names. Annotating any or unknown silences the rule and leaves the contract \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bmissing.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153msrc/domain/command.ts:46:7 ERROR @typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  Missing return type on function.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m "]
